{"id":"osnovanie","lemma":"основание","pos":"noun","rank":4647,"glosses":["base, foundation, pedestal","foundation, establishment","grounds, reason, argument"],"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/6/65/Ru-%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B5.ogg/Ru-%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%B5.ogg.mp3","gender":"n","forms":{"genitive":"основания","plural":"основания"},"examples":[{"text":"Есть основания для оптимизма.","en":"There are grounds for optimism.","words":[{"g":"there is / to eat"},null,{"g":"for"},null]},{"text":"У него были все основания так поступить.","en":"He had every reason for doing so.","words":[{"g":"at / by"},{"g":"he, it","l":"он"},{"g":"were","l":"быть"},{"g":"everyone, everybody"},null,{"g":"so"},{"g":"to act"}]},{"text":"Том изменил всё до основания.","en":"Tom changed everything from the ground up.","words":[{"g":"that one, those ones","l":"тот"},{"g":"to change","l":"изменить"},{"g":"everything, all"},{"g":"until / before"},null]},{"text":"У меня были основания для ревности.","en":"I had good reason to be jealous.","words":[{"g":"at / by"},{"g":"me","l":"я"},{"g":"were","l":"быть"},null,{"g":"for"},{"g":"jealousy","l":"ревность"}]},{"text":"У него есть все основания гордиться сыном.","en":"He's every reason to be proud of his son.","words":[{"g":"at / by"},{"g":"he, it","l":"он"},{"g":"there is / to eat"},{"g":"everyone, everybody"},null,{"g":"to be proud"},{"g":"son","l":"сын"}]}]}